@page "/system"
@model SystemModel
@{ ViewData["Title"] = "System health"; }
<div class="page-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">THIS DASHBOARD INSTANCE</div><h1>System health</h1><p>Dependency checks and local monitoring configuration.</p></div><a class="button" asp-page="/System">↻ Refresh</a></div>
<section class="card detail-card"><div class="card-heading"><h2>@(Model.Stopping ? "Stopping" : Model.Health.Ready ? "Ready" : "Dependencies unavailable")</h2><span class="muted">Checked · @Display.Time(Model.Health.CheckedAt) UTC</span></div>
<dl class="facts"><div><dt>Metadata access</dt><dd>@(Model.Health.MetadataReady ? "Ready" : "Unavailable")</dd></div><div><dt>Replay connection</dt><dd>@(Model.Health.ReplayReady is null ? "Disabled" : Model.Health.ReplayReady.Value ? "Ready" : "Unavailable")</dd></div><div><dt>Prometheus endpoint</dt><dd>@(Model.MetricsEnabled ? "Enabled · bearer token required" : "Disabled")</dd></div><div><dt>Instance started · UTC</dt><dd>@Display.Time(Model.StartedAt)</dd></div><div><dt>HTTP responses since startup</dt><dd>@Model.Requests</dd></div></dl>
<p class="data-note">Checks share a five-second cache and bounded database access. Ready confirms the configured schema/profile checks; it does not guarantee every permission or the success of the next transaction. Counts reset when this instance restarts.</p></section>
<section class="notice"><h2>@(Model.WorkersConfigured ? "Worker monitoring is configured" : "Worker monitoring is not connected to this panel")</h2><p>Your application runs consumers and outbox dispatchers separately. Dashboard health and HTTP response counts do not measure event processing speed, backlog or broker availability.</p><p><a asp-page="/Workers">Open worker monitoring</a> to check target freshness, running loops and recent cycle observations. Business throughput and backlog are not inferred from these signals.</p></section>
